Subject: [PATCH] d3d9: report the runtime's matrix palette for indexed vertex blending

The UMD reported MaxVertexBlendMatrixIndex 0, which says indexed vertex
blending is not available with hardware vertex processing, so applications
that check the cap switch to software vertex processing for it. The D3D9
runtime does support it on this UMD: it turns the fixed-function state into
a vs_2_0 shader that picks world matrices by index from the constants
(base c175, 8 registers per matrix, as its SetVertexShaderConst calls and
generated shader show). That leaves room for matrices 0 to 8 in 256
constants, and the runtime uploads none above 8, so a vertex with index 9
or more is transformed by unset constants.

Report 8: indices 0 to 8 render as on the reference rasterizer with
hardware vertex processing; applications that need more still fall back to
software vertex processing, which supports 256 matrices.

Evidence: docs/ffp2.md, docs/evidence/ffp2/ (src/d3d9_ffp2.cpp,
vb_indexed_*).
Origin: vmlab-win3d ffp2 worker.
---
diff --git a/src/gallium/frontends/d3d10umd/D3D9Adapter.cpp b/src/gallium/frontends/d3d10umd/D3D9Adapter.cpp
index 52ce2f7..d99ea58 100644
--- a/src/gallium/frontends/d3d10umd/D3D9Adapter.cpp
+++ b/src/gallium/frontends/d3d10umd/D3D9Adapter.cpp
@@ -188,7 +188,13 @@ D3D9FillCaps(const D3D9Adapter *adapter, D3DCAPS9 *caps)
    caps->MaxActiveLights = 0x00000008;
    caps->MaxUserClipPlanes = 0x00000008;
    caps->MaxVertexBlendMatrices = 0x00000004;
-   caps->MaxVertexBlendMatrixIndex = 0x00000000;
+   /* With hardware vertex processing the runtime turns indexed vertex
+    * blending into a vs_2_0 shader that keeps world matrices 0 to 8 in the
+    * constants from c175, 8 registers each, and uploads no higher matrix.
+    * That palette works; 0 told applications there was none, so they fell
+    * back to software vertex processing. Applications that need higher
+    * indices still have to. */
+   caps->MaxVertexBlendMatrixIndex = 8;
    caps->MaxPointSize = D3D9FloatFromBits(0x46000000);
    caps->MaxPrimitiveCount = 0x007fffff;
    caps->MaxVertexIndex = 0x00ffffff;
